<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-multiply" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Multiplying Fractions</title>

  <p> When multiplying fractions, the numerators are multiplied to give the result's numerator, and the denominators are multiplied to give the result's denominator; 
  <md>\frac{a}{c}\times\frac{b}{d}=\frac{ab}{cd}.</md></p>

  <example>
    <title>Multiplying Fractions</title>
    <statement>
      <p>
        Calculate <m>\frac{5}{7}\times\frac{4}{9}</m>.
      </p>
    </statement>
    <solution>
      <p>
        Multiplying the numerators and denominators gives 
         <md>\frac{5}{7}\times\frac{4}{9}=\frac{5\times 4}{7\times 9}=\frac{20}{63}.</md>
         This is in reduced form.
      </p>
    
    </solution>
  </example>

  <exercise label="ww-fraction-multiplication">
    <title>Multiplying Fractions</title>
    <webwork>
        <pg-code>
            # Set the math environment to expect fraction format answers
            Context("Fraction-NoDecimals");
            
            # Define the exact answer
            $ans = Fraction(8,15);
        </pg-code>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Evaluate the following expression. 
                Provide your answer as a reduced fraction.
            </p>
            <p>
                <m>\frac{8}{9} \times \frac{3}{5} = </m> <var name="$ans" width="10"/>
            </p>
        </statement>
    </webwork>
</exercise>

